Two way to create a branch of a repository.
The first way is to use git checkout [branch-name].
The second way to create a branch is to use git branch [branch-name].

Create a replica of a repository, the copy is named test-branch,  
and switch to newly created replica branch named test-branch.
axruf@axruffin MINGW64 ~/github/Azure-Deployment-Using-bicep-files/Git Concepts and Config (main) <----
$ git checkout test-branch
We switch branches.
axruf@axruffin MINGW64 ~/github/Azure-Deployment-Using-bicep-files/Git Concepts and Config (test-branch) <----  

Or  

Create a replica of a repository and the copy is named test-branch.
axruf@axruffin MINGW64 ~/github/Azure-Deployment-Using-bicep-files/Git Concepts and Config (main) <----
$ git branch test-branch
We did not switch branches.
